+### Select controls
+
+`select` supports native `<select>` elements and standard ARIA `combobox` and `listbox` controls. Option matching is exact against the value, label, or whitespace-normalized accessible text. The command uses browser input to open and choose custom widgets, types into input-backed combobox filters when needed, waits for dynamically rendered associated options, and verifies selected state, the committed combobox display/value, or an associated standard form value. A single-select native or ARIA control accepts one value. Native multiple selects retain multi-value behavior; multiple ARIA values require `aria-multiselectable="true"` on an ARIA listbox and are treated as the final desired set. Unknown, disabled, hidden, unsupported, or unverifiable controls return an error. The wait is bounded by the configured default action timeout. The action uses CDP-managed browser sessions; WebDriver backends report it as unsupported.
